#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/11
msgid ""
"I joined NASA - got to do the kind of research I\n"
"loved.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/12
msgid ""
"Our nation's prestige hinged on our work.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/13
msgid ""
"They gave us whatever resources we asked for.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/14
msgid ""
"I knew you could turn a rocket into an ICBM by\n"
"fitting it with a nuclear warhead,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/242/0xf2c30/17
msgid "7^"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/0
msgid ""
"But you know... there's something I've never been\n"
"able to figure out.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你知道……有件事我一直\n"
"想不明白。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/1
msgid ""
"Is the Cold War really a war, or is it really peace...?\n"
msgstr ""
"冷战究竟是战争，还是和平……？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/2
msgid ""
"Doc, what are you...?\n"
msgstr ""
"博士，你在……？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/3
msgid ""
"People called it a \"cold war,\" but I disagreed.\n"
msgstr ""
"人们称之为\"冷战\"，但我不同意。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/4
msgid ""
"Sure, nuclear stockpiles are increasing, threats are\n"
"multiplying,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错，核武库在增加，威胁在\n"
"倍增，\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/5
msgid ""
"the U.S. and the Soviet Union have enough power\n"
msgstr ""
"美苏两国的力量足以\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/6
msgid ""
"to destroy the human race a hundred times over.\n"
msgstr ""
"毁灭人类上百次。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/7
msgid ""
"But nobody's actually being killed. Small-scale\n"
"conflicts and proxy wars, maybe...\n"
msgstr ""
"但实际没人被杀。小规模\n"
"冲突和代理人战争，也许……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/8
msgid ""
"But nuclear deterrence has averted another world\n"
"war.\n"
msgstr ""
"但核威慑避免了另一场世界\n"
"大战。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/9
msgid ""
"The world's far more peaceful today than it was\n"
"before.\n"
msgstr ""
"如今的世界比以往\n"
"和平得多。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/10
msgid ""
"And the breakthroughs we've made in space\n"
"exploration\n"
msgstr ""
"还有我们在太空探索方面\n"
"取得的突破\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/11
msgid ""
"thanks to Cold War competition - fantastic, don't\n"
"you think?\n"
msgstr ""
"多亏冷战竞争——太棒了，你不\n"
"觉得吗？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/12
msgid ""
"No... We didn't need to rush into space like that...\n"
msgstr ""
"不……我们不该那样急着进太空……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/13
msgid ""
"Going into space may have been mankind's dream,\n"
msgstr ""
"进入太空也许是人类的梦想，\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/14
msgid ""
"but good people were sacrificed in the scramble.\n"
msgstr ""
"但在这场争夺中好人被牺牲了。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/15
msgid ""
"...Maybe so. NASA's definitely got some skeletons in\n"
"its closet...\n"
msgstr ""
"……也许吧。NASA确实有些见不得\n"
"人的秘密……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/16
msgid ""
"Same goes for the nuclear arms race.\n"
msgstr ""
"核军备竞赛也一样。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/17
msgid ""
"Atomic testing has killed civilians and exposed\n"
"thousands to radiation.\n"
msgstr ""
"核试验害死了平民，让数千人\n"
"暴露在辐射中。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/18
msgid ""
"Believe me, I know...\n"
msgstr ""
"相信我，我知道……\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/19
msgid ""
"And now this... What peace was I trying to protect,\n"
"anyway?\n"
msgstr ""
"而现在这个……我到底是想守护怎样的和平，\n"
"话说回来？\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf34f0/20
msgid ""
"The more I think about it, the less I understand.\n"
msgstr ""
"越想越不明白。\n"

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/0
msgid ""
"Let's speak in hypotheticals for a minute.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/1
msgid ""
"Say you wanted to make a clone of yourself...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/2
msgid ""
"A clone? Para-Medic had the same idea. It's\n"
"science fiction.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/3
msgid ""
"I'm just hypothesizing here. OK, not a clone, then.\n"
"You have any kids?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/4
msgid ""
"Nope.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/5
msgid ""
"Wife?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/6
msgid ""
"...Never been tied down.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/7
msgid ""
"OK, then... so we're still talking hypotheticals.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/8
msgid ""
"Say you had a son who'd inherited your genes,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/9
msgid ""
"someone with the same combat abilities as you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/10
msgid ""
"Would you challenge him to a fight?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/11
msgid ""
"...Hmm. Not to sound cocky, but I wouldn't want to\n"
"do that. No telling who'd survive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/12
msgid ""
"I'll bet. You picked up on the Pupa-5000's combat\n"
"patterns in seconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/13
msgid ""
"Only with your advice, Doc.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/14
msgid ""
"If anybody could learn to do it just by listening, it'd\n"
"be easy.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/15
msgid ""
"But you - you're a born soldier.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/18
msgid "<~"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/243/0xf3c40/29
msgid "ո"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/0
msgid ""
"Nuclear deterrence means preventing the use of\n"
"nuclear weapons\n"
msgstr ""
"核威慑意味着防止在\n"
"国家间冲突中使用核武器\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 1421..2661
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/1
msgid ""
"in conflicts between states. But what about other\n"
"situations?\n"
msgstr ""
"在国家间的冲突中。但其他\n"
"情况又如何呢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 2953..3761
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/3
msgid ""
"Terrorism has been on the rise in recent years,\n"
msgstr ""
"近年来恐怖主义不断抬头，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 3761..4736
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/4
msgid ""
"from separatist movements to far-left extremists.\n"
msgstr ""
"从分离主义运动到极左极端分子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 4736..6018
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/5
msgid ""
"What would happen if nuclear weapons fell into\n"
"terrorist hands?\n"
msgstr ""
"如果核武器落入恐怖分子手中\n"
"会怎样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 6018..7091
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/6
msgid ""
"Without a state - that is, without territory of their\n"
"own\n"
msgstr ""
"没有国家，即没有自己的\n"
"领土\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 7091..8080
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/7
msgid ""
"- the chances of having nukes used against them\n"
"are slim.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 他们遭核武打击的可能性\n"
"微乎其微。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 8122..8958
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/8
msgid ""
"They have no reason to fear a nuclear strike.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们没理由害怕核打击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 9000..10476
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/9
msgid ""
"Conversely, they have no reason to hesitate to use\n"
"nukes against their adversaries.\n"
msgstr ""
"反过来，他们也没理由犹豫\n"
"对敌动用核武。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 10476..11633
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/10
msgid ""
"You've got a point. All the ICBMs and strategic\n"
"bombers in the world\n"
msgstr ""
"有道理。世上所有洲际导弹和战略\n"
"轰炸机\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 11633..12260
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/11
msgid ""
"amount to nothing against a terrorist group.\n"
msgstr ""
"对恐怖组织都毫无用处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 12260..13318
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/12
msgid ""
"Right! Of course, this is all still hypothetical.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错！当然，这些都还只是假设。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 13360..13959
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/13
msgid ""
"Countries keep their nukes under tight watch\n"
msgstr ""
"各国对核武看管严密\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 13959..15032
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/14
msgid ""
"- there's no immediate danger of terrorists getting\n"
"their hands on them.\n"
msgstr ""
"- 目前不存在恐怖分子\n"
"获得这些武器的直接危险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 15032..16021
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/15
msgid ""
"But the day may come when the proposition of\n"
"nuclear terrorism\n"
msgstr ""
"但总有一天，核恐怖主义\n"
"可能成真\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 16021..16885
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/16
msgid ""
"makes nuclear deterrence theory a dead letter.\n"
msgstr ""
"会让核威慑理论彻底失效。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 16885..18125
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/17
msgid ""
"Nuclear terrorism... Interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"核恐怖主义……有意思。\n"

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/0
msgid ""
"What are we going to do, Snake? If Peace Walker\n"
"attacks Mother Base...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/1
msgid ""
"Relax. We've got the entire MSF out to make sure\n"
"that doesn't happen.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, but... Peace Walker's missiles have\n"
"one-megaton warheads.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/3
msgid ""
"The fireball alone'd be a mile in diameter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/4
msgid ""
"Everything in the vicinity of ground zero will be\n"
"vaporized by the heat rays.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/36
msgid "񋜱"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/44
msgid ""
"˱\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/244/0xf4d90/47
msgid "5/"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/0
msgid ""
"I gotta say... I'm surprised you helped us arm Metal\n"
"Gear with Nukes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/1
msgid ""
"What of it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/2
msgid ""
"Don't get me wrong, I'm grateful and all, but... you\n"
"sure about this?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/3
msgid ""
"They may be for MSF's self-defense, but they're\n"
"still nukes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/245/0xf5e40/4
msgid ""
"It's essentially the same thing as Peace Walker,\n"
"which you despised.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 431..2340
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/0
msgid ""
"The aim of the Peace Walker Project is to achieve\n"
"robust nuclear deterrence across Central America\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者计划的目标是在中美洲全境\n"
"实现强力核威慑\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3538
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/1
msgid ""
"by deploying a new nuclear weapon system along\n"
"the Caribbean coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"方式是在加勒比沿岸部署\n"
"新型核武器系统。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4430
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/2
msgid ""
"Peace Walker is also the name of the system itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者也是这套系统本身的名称。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 4639..6213
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/3
msgid ""
"A nuclear weapon named \"Peace\"... I can just see\n"
"the look on Kaz's face.\n"
msgstr ""
"名为“和平”的核武……我能想象\n"
"卡兹的表情。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 6241..7300
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/4
msgid ""
"So why exactly does this new system need legs in\n"
"the first place?\n"
msgstr ""
"那么，这个新系统究竟为什么\n"
"首先需要腿呢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 7300..7704
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/5
msgid ""
"Because it's a \"Walker.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"因为它是“行者”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 7704..8094
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/6
msgid ""
"An unmanned weapon\n"
msgstr ""
"无人武器\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 8094..9613
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/7
msgid ""
"moving under its own power and capable of\n"
"launching a deterrent strike from anywhere...\n"
msgstr ""
"自行移动，能从任何地方\n"
"发动威慑打击……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0070_000_0
#. timeline 9738..10671
#: codec/1/246/0xf6670/8
msgid ""
"That's the whole idea behind Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是和平行者的全部构想。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 459..1476
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/0
msgid ""
"The reason Peace Walker is a mobile nuclear\n"
"weapons system\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者之所以是移动式核\n"
"武器系统\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 1476..2452
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/1
msgid ""
"is to maximize its potential as a nuclear deterrent.\n"
msgstr ""
"是为了最大化其核威慑潜力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 2730..3873
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/3
msgid ""
"If need be, Peace Walker can stay constantly on\n"
"the move\n"
msgstr ""
"必要时，和平行者可以不停\n"
"移动\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 3873..4764
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/4
msgid ""
"so that the adversary can't pinpoint its position...\n"
msgstr ""
"让敌人无法锁定其位置……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5684
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/5
msgid ""
"That allows it to avoid preemptive enemy strikes.\n"
msgstr ""
"从而避免遭敌方先发制人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 5684..6645
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/6
msgid ""
"So you're saying it keeps the retaliation card in\n"
"play.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你是说它会保留报复卡在\n"
"手牌中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 6645..7397
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/7
msgid ""
"Coldman likes to brag about it in this way...\n"
msgstr ""
"科尔德曼就爱这么吹嘘……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 7397..8219
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/8
msgid ""
"Like a land-based version of an SSBN.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像陆基版的战略核潜艇。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 8233..9013
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/9
msgid ""
"And there's another reason for them to be mobile.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们能移动还有另一个原因。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 9097..10184
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/10
msgid ""
"Peace Walker also has a self-destruct function.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者还有自毁功能。\n"

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/0
msgid ""
"Why would Peace Walker need a self-destruct\n"
"function?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/1
msgid ""
"You saw it, didn't you, Snake? That sphere on\n"
"Peace Walker's head?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/3
msgid ""
"That's a hydrogen bomb.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/4
msgid ""
"What?! You're telling me that thing's a\n"
"thermonuclear device?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/5
msgid ""
"Do they have any idea what kind of destruction\n"
"that thing would cause...?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/6
msgid ""
"I know, it's crazy. I mean, even overkill has its\n"
"limits.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/7
msgid ""
"If it's strategic value they want, they could have\n"
"gone with something smaller.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/246/0xf6dc0/11
msgid "tN5.Lʧ"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 459..2145
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/0
msgid ""
"The biggest nuclear warhead ever actually\n"
"detonated was the Soviet RDS-220,\n"
msgstr ""
"实际引爆过最大的核弹头\n"
"是苏联RDS-220，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 2173..2828
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/1
msgid ""
"nicknamed \"Tsar Bomba.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"绰号“沙皇炸弹”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 2828..3914
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/2
msgid ""
"It had an estimated yield of 57 megatons\n"
msgstr ""
"当量估计达5700万吨\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 3942..5363
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/3
msgid ""
"- ten times as much power as all the explosives\n"
"used throughout World War II.\n"
msgstr ""
"——威力是整个二战期间使用的所有炸药的\n"
"十倍。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 5391..6924
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/4
msgid ""
"The test took place on October 30, 1961, above\n"
"Novaya Zemlya.\n"
msgstr ""
"试验于1961年10月30日在新地岛\n"
"上空进行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 6979..8331
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/5
msgid ""
"The explosion is believed to have created a fireball\n"
"over two miles in diameter.\n"
msgstr ""
"据信爆炸产生的火球\n"
"直径超过两英里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 8359..9431
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/6
msgid ""
"Can you believe that? Like a miniature sun.\n"
msgstr ""
"你敢信吗？就像一颗微型太阳。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 9473..10992
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/7
msgid ""
"The explosion was seen as far off as Finland - 600\n"
"miles away\n"
msgstr ""
"爆炸远至芬兰都能看到，600\n"
"英里外\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 11006..11842
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/8
msgid ""
"- and some people even reported windows\n"
"shattering.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有人报告说窗户\n"
"被震碎了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 11870..12803
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/9
msgid ""
"The shockwave traveled three times around the\n"
"earth.\n"
msgstr ""
"冲击波环绕地球\n"
"三圈。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 12803..13221
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/10
msgid ""
"Three times?\n"
msgstr ""
"三圈？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 13221..14238
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/11
msgid ""
"Peace Walker is armed with a massive hydrogen\n"
"bomb\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者装备了一枚巨大的氢\n"
"弹\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 14238..14976
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/12
msgid ""
"even more destructive than Tsar Bomba.\n"
msgstr ""
"破坏力比沙皇炸弹还大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 14976..15868
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/13
msgid ""
"It can sneak into enemy territory, lie low,\n"
msgstr ""
"它能潜入敌境、隐蔽待命，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 15882..17428
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/14
msgid ""
"and - in the event of an enemy nuclear strike -\n"
"detonate itself in retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""
"并且——在敌方发动核打击时——\n"
"会自行引爆进行报复。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 17526..18306
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/15
msgid ""
"And the locomotion system that lets it do that...\n"
msgstr ""
"而让它做到这些的行走系统……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 18306..18780
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/16
msgid ""
"...My research...\n"
msgstr ""
"……我的研究……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 18780..20006
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/17
msgid ""
"...Snake, those legs were supposed to make my\n"
"dream come true.\n"
msgstr ""
"……Snake，那双腿本应让我的\n"
"梦想成真。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 20006..21413
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/18
msgid ""
"Now they're about to jump the fence of nuclear\n"
"deterrence. You have to stop them!\n"
msgstr ""
"现在它们即将越过核威慑的\n"
"栅栏。你必须阻止它们！\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 21413..22736
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/19
msgid ""
"I'll apply all my energy into developing weapons and\n"
"equipment to help you do it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会倾注全部精力开发武器和\n"
"装备来帮你做到。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_020_1
#. timeline 22736..23224
#: codec/1/247/0xf7300/20
msgid ""
"Sounds like a deal.\n"
msgstr ""
"成交。\n"

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/0
msgid ""
"What made you put an AI into Peace Walker?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/1
msgid ""
"Well, for one thing, because it can't be manned.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/2
msgid ""
"Peace Walker's designed to enter enemy territory\n"
"and blow itself up - if necessary.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/3
msgid ""
"You can't put a person inside a weapon that could\n"
"blow at anytime, can you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/4
msgid ""
"So we equipped it with an AI instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/5
msgid ""
"That's... strangely humane of you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/6
msgid ""
"And besides, Peace Walker was designed as a\n"
"bipedal weapons system.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/7
msgid ""
"You can't imagine how hard it shakes when it\n"
"walks. It'd turn a man into mush.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/8
msgid ""
"Plus, when launching a nuclear missile,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/9
msgid ""
"it has to perform ballistic calculations in real time,\n"
"see?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/10
msgid ""
"Because it's always moving.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/11
msgid ""
"Hold on. If that's all it does, then a\n"
"high-performance computer ought to do the job.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/12
msgid ""
"It doesn't need intelligence.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/13
msgid ""
"That's a very good point, Snake. Which brings me\n"
"to the real reason...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/14
msgid ""
"Peace Walker needs AI to make decisions\n"
"regarding nuclear retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/15
msgid ""
"It's what ensures perfectly mutual assured\n"
"destruction.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/16
msgid ""
"I've heard all of this before. You want a war\n"
"between machines?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/17
msgid ""
"We'd never actually launch the first nuke, of\n"
"course.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/18
msgid ""
"It's strictly a counterattack system.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/19
msgid ""
"Only a politician could make such an illogical\n"
"decision as starting a nuclear war.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/20
msgid ""
"Conversely, if an adversary launches a nuke at us,\n"
"the AI will not fail to retaliate.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/247/0xf7a40/34
msgid "8"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 445..1490
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/0
msgid ""
"Peace Walker is fitted with several close-range\n"
"weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者装了几种近程\n"
"武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 1504..2758
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/1
msgid ""
"We'd also planned for it to be able to enter enemy\n"
"territory and self-detonate.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们还计划让它能进入敌方\n"
"领地自爆。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 2814..3761
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/2
msgid ""
"Wonderful. What exactly are we dealing with here?\n"
msgstr ""
"好极了。具体要对付什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 3803..5154
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/3
msgid ""
"Well, the flamethrowers, for one thing - One in the\n"
"front, and one in the rear.\n"
msgstr ""
"首先是火焰喷射器——一个在\n"
"前面，一个在后面。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 5210..6952
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/4
msgid ""
"Then there are the S-mines. They're like cluster\n"
"bombs. It scatters them from its leg hatches.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有S型地雷。像集束\n"
"炸弹，从腿部舱口撒出来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 6979..7787
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/5
msgid ""
"If you see those open, you'd better clear out\n"
"quickly.\n"
msgstr ""
"看到那些舱口打开，最好赶紧\n"
"闪开。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 7815..9278
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/6
msgid ""
"And finally, the rockets. These can travel quite a\n"
"distance, so stay sharp.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后是火箭弹。射程相当\n"
"远，保持警惕。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 9306..10323
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/7
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it can't fire them from too\n"
"close...\n"
msgstr ""
"不过它没法在太近的\n"
"距离发射……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 10379..11131
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/8
msgid ""
"but then again there are those flamethrowers.\n"
msgstr ""
"但别忘了还有火焰喷射器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 11173..12343
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/9
msgid ""
"It can also use its legs as weapons against any\n"
"infantry on the ground.\n"
msgstr ""
"它还能用腿攻击地面上的\n"
"步兵。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 12357..12538
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/10
msgid ""
"Ouch.\n"
msgstr ""
"疼啊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 12552..13681
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/11
msgid ""
"But remember, Peace Walker technically isn't\n"
"complete.\n"
msgstr ""
"但记住，和平行者严格来说还没\n"
"完成。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 13736..15046
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/12
msgid ""
"With just the Reptile Pod, it can only perform\n"
"relatively simple maneuvers.\n"
msgstr ""
"只有爬虫舱时，它只能做\n"
"相对简单的动作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 15116..15715
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/13
msgid ""
"They've got certain quirks too.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们还有些怪癖。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 15770..16370
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/14
msgid ""
"What's more, look carefully\n"
msgstr ""
"而且，仔细看\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0035_000_0
#. timeline 16370..17401
#: codec/1/248/0xf87b0/15
msgid ""
"and you should be able to predict which attack is\n"
"coming next.\n"
msgstr ""
"应该能预判下一招是\n"
"什么。\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/0
msgid ""
"Snake! You have to stop Peace Walker from\n"
"launching that nuke!\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE！你得阻止和平行者\n"
"发射核弹！\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/1
msgid ""
"Calm down. What do I need to do?\n"
msgstr ""
"冷静。我该怎么做？\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/2
msgid ""
"To tell you the truth, I don't really know...\n"
msgstr ""
"说实话，我也不太清楚……\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/3
msgid ""
"The Mammal Pod has probably enhanced both its\n"
"thought patterns and mobility.\n"
msgstr ""
"哺乳舱可能强化了它的\n"
"思维和机动性。\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/4
msgid ""
"The S-mines, rockets, flamethrowers - they're all\n"
"the same, but\n"
msgstr ""
"S型地雷、火箭弹、火焰喷射器，都\n"
"一样，但\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/5
msgid ""
"I don't know what else to say...\n"
msgstr ""
"不知还能说啥……\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/6
msgid ""
"You'll just have to stay sharp and watch for how it\n"
"behaves before each of the attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"你只能保持警惕，观察它每次\n"
"攻击前的动作。\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/7
msgid ""
"I'll give it a shot. There's no time for anything else.\n"
msgstr ""
"我试试。没时间想别的了。\n"

#: codec/1/248/0xf8da0/8
msgid ""
"Sorry I can't be more helpful. You can do it, Snake!\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉帮不上更多忙。你能行的，SNAKE！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 445..1504
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/0
msgid ""
"OK, but why does Peace Walker need to walk on\n"
"two legs?\n"
msgstr ""
"好吧，但为什么和平行者需要用\n"
"两条腿走路？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 1560..2117
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/1
msgid ""
"I'd think treads would be good enough.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得履带就够用了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 2131..2633
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/2
msgid ""
"You'd be wrong.\n"
msgstr ""
"你错了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 2661..3845
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/3
msgid ""
"As you know, the terrain in Central America is\n"
"rugged and complex.\n"
msgstr ""
"如你所知，中美洲的地形\n"
"崎岖而复杂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 3873..4764
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/4
msgid ""
"Especially along the Caribbean coast of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是哥斯达黎加的加勒比沿岸。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 4778..5753
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/5
msgid ""
"You've got jungles, swamps, mountains...\n"
msgstr ""
"有丛林、沼泽、山地……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 5767..7147
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/6
msgid ""
"And the only way to get across all that terrain, no\n"
"matter how rugged, is on legs.\n"
msgstr ""
"穿越所有这些地形，无论\n"
"多崎岖，只能靠腿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 7216..8205
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/7
msgid ""
"But wouldn't it be tough to cross a swamp even on\n"
"legs?\n"
msgstr ""
"但靠腿穿过沼泽不也很\n"
"难吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 8233..8888
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/8
msgid ""
"It wasn't easy, that's for sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"确实不容易。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 8930..9668
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/9
msgid ""
"The reason we picked Costa Rica as a proving\n"
"ground\n"
msgstr ""
"我们选哥斯达黎加当试验场的\n"
"原因\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0100_000_0
#. timeline 9668..10644
#: codec/1/249/0xf9120/10
msgid ""
"is because we can test it on every type of terrain.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是因为能在各种地形上测试。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 459..2061
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/0
msgid ""
"This \"Peace Walker Project\" the CIA's talking about\n"
"- you believed in it, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA所说的这个“和平行者计划”\n"
"——你相信过它，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 2089..3678
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/1
msgid ""
"Yeah. I believed... Actually, maybe I just wanted to\n"
"believe.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。我相信过……其实，也许我只是想\n"
"相信。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 4026..5614
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/3
msgid ""
"Here's how Coldman explained it. Peace Walker's a\n"
"weapon for peace,\n"
msgstr ""
"考德曼这样解释。和平行者是种\n"
"和平武器，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6548
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/4
msgid ""
"one to ensure true nuclear deterrence.\n"
msgstr ""
"用来确保真正的核威慑。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 6589..7606
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/5
msgid ""
"It'd be the anchor to bring stability to Central\n"
"America...\n"
msgstr ""
"它将成为给中美洲带来稳定的\n"
"支柱……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 7620..9195
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/6
msgid ""
"He told me, \"The nuclear weapons system you've\n"
"built will never be used.\n"
msgstr ""
"他对我说：“你建造的核武器系统\n"
"永远不会被使用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 9209..10323
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/7
msgid ""
"It will forever stand vigil as an icon of peace.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"它将永远作为和平的图标守望。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 10337..11647
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/8
msgid ""
"And to achieve that, he needed my bipedal\n"
"locomotion technology...\n"
msgstr ""
"为此，他需要我的双足\n"
"行走技术……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 11772..12399
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/9
msgid ""
"To be honest, I was flattered.\n"
msgstr ""
"说实话，我挺得意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 12413..12733
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/10
msgid ""
"Flattered?\n"
msgstr ""
"得意？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 12747..13137
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/11
msgid ""
"Wouldn't you be?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不会吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 13165..14363
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/12
msgid ""
"My colleagues in the scientific community have\n"
"never taken me seriously.\n"
msgstr ""
"我在科学界的同事们从来\n"
"没有认真对待过我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 14391..15868
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/13
msgid ""
"They told me bipedal locomotion was a pipe dream,\n"
"that it'd never amount to anything.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们告诉我双足行走是白日做梦，\n"
"永远不会有什么成果。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 15882..16815
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/14
msgid ""
"It was the first time anybody recognized my work...\n"
msgstr ""
"那是第一次有人认可我的研究……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 16885..17944
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/15
msgid ""
"How could I not be happy? And besides...\n"
msgstr ""
"我怎能不高兴？而且……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 17944..18724
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/16
msgid ""
"It was my chance to surpass my father.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是我超越父亲的机会。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 18836..20131
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/17
msgid ""
"To create nukes for peace... Or so I thought,\n"
"anyway.\n"
msgstr ""
"为了和平而制造核弹……至少我当时是这么想的。\n"
"反正。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 20131..20828
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/18
msgid ""
"But Coldman's really going through with it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但科尔德曼真要动手了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 20828..21775
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/19
msgid ""
"Yeah. Makes perfect sense, really.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，完全说得通。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 21873..23684
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/20
msgid ""
"No one would give the project any notice unless\n"
"they could prove that an unmanned system is\n"
"capable of launching a nuke.\n"
msgstr ""
"没人会注意到这个项目，除非\n"
"他们能证明一个无人系统\n"
"有能力发射核弹。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 445..1100
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/0
msgid ""
"Why is Coldman gonna launch a nuke?\n"
msgstr ""
"科尔德曼为啥发射核弹？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 1100..2173
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/1
msgid ""
"If all he wants to do is prove the AI retaliation\n"
"system works,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果他只是想证明AI报复\n"
"系统有效，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 2187..2939
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/2
msgid ""
"he doesn't need to put a live warhead on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"根本不需要装实弹头。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 2939..4277
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/3
msgid ""
"I agree. He could demonstrate the system by\n"
"launching the missile alone\n"
msgstr ""
"我同意。他可以通过\n"
"单独发射导弹来演示这个系统\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 4277..5349
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/4
msgid ""
"- without a warhead. I asked him the same thing at\n"
"first.\n"
msgstr ""
"没弹头。我一开始也问过他同样\n"
"问题。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 5363..6213
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/5
msgid ""
"He said there was no point in using a dummy\n"
"missile...\n"
msgstr ""
"他说用假弹\n"
"没有意义……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 6283..7592
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/6
msgid ""
"That it'd take an actual nuclear launch to deter\n"
"potential enemies.\n"
msgstr ""
"只有真正的核发射才能威慑\n"
"潜在的敌人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 7592..8860
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/7
msgid ""
"Launching the real deal gives him a leg up in\n"
"negotiations with Langley.\n"
msgstr ""
"发射真家伙能让他在\n"
"与兰利的谈判中占上风。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0110_010_0
#. timeline 8902..9445
#: codec/1/249/0xf9c50/8
msgid ""
"That's what he's really after.\n"
msgstr ""
"那才是他真正目的。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/0
msgid ""
"How'd you get your hands on Granin's research?\n"
msgstr ""
"你怎么拿到格拉宁的研究？\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/1
msgid ""
"That was also Coldman. He used his Agency\n"
"contacts to get a hold of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"那也是科尔曼。他利用自己在机构的\n"
"人脉搞到了它。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/2
msgid ""
"Giving you stolen information then using it to\n"
"blackmail you... Damn.\n"
msgstr ""
"先给你偷来的情报，再用它来\n"
"敲诈你……该死。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/3
msgid ""
"I knew it was Granin's work the minute I saw it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我一看就知道是格拉宁的成果。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/4
msgid ""
"See, I'd been corresponding with him for a while.\n"
msgstr ""
"我跟他通信有一阵子了。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/5
msgid ""
"Corresponding?\n"
msgstr ""
"通信？\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/6
msgid ""
"Letters. Between scientists doing the same kind of\n"
"research...\n"
msgstr ""
"信件。在从事同类\n"
"研究的科学家之间……\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/7
msgid ""
"He always complained that nobody understood his\n"
"ideas on bipedal locomotion.\n"
msgstr ""
"他总是抱怨没人理解他\n"
"关于双足行走的想法。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/8
msgid ""
"Ah... So you're the \"American friend\" he was talking\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""
"啊……所以你就是他所说的那个“美国\n"
"朋友”。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/9
msgid ""
"Obviously he didn't write a word about the\n"
"technology in his letters.\n"
msgstr ""
"显然，他在信里对这项技术\n"
"一个字都没写。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/10
msgid ""
"Except for one time.\n"
msgstr ""
"只有一次。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/11
msgid ""
"\"If by chance anything should happen to me, I\n"
"entrust my research to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"“万一我出了什么事，\n"
"我的研究就托付给你了。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/12
msgid ""
"Better that than handing it over to these ignorant\n"
"so-called scientists.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"总比交给那些无知的\n"
"所谓科学家强。”\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/13
msgid ""
"Sounds like him, all right.\n"
msgstr ""
"确实像他的口气。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/14
msgid ""
"Then one day his papers actually came.\n"
msgstr ""
"后来有天，论文真寄来了。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/15
msgid ""
"It wasn't hard for me to imagine what had\n"
"happened to him.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不难想象他\n"
"遭遇了什么。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/16
msgid ""
"I felt it was my duty to carry on his work after\n"
"him... And also...\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得有责任继承他的研究……\n"
"而且……\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/18
msgid ""
"I thought maybe combining his technology with\n"
"mine\n"
msgstr ""
"我想也许把他的技术\n"
"和我的结合起来\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/19
msgid ""
"could be a way to bring East and West together.\n"
msgstr ""
"能让东西方走到一起。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/20
msgid ""
"Like the docking of Apollo and Soyuz.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像阿波罗和联盟号对接。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/21
msgid ""
"It'll never make the history books. And it's still not\n"
"a reason to plagiarize.\n"
msgstr ""
"这永远不会载入史册。而且这仍然不是\n"
"抄袭的理由。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/22
msgid ""
"...You're right. You're absolutely right.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你说得对。完全正确。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/23
msgid ""
"I never had the courage to tell the truth, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""
"我只是从没勇气说出真相。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/24
msgid ""
"I always looked for excuses to cover it up.\n"
msgstr ""
"我总在找借口掩盖。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/25
msgid ""
"Until now.\n"
msgstr ""
"直到现在。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/26
msgid ""
"Huh...?\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯？\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfa640/27
msgid ""
"You told me everything. You're no longer a coward.\n"
msgstr ""
"你全说出来了。你不再是懦夫了。\n"

#: codec/1/250/0xfaf50/0
msgid ""
"\"Metal Gear\"...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfaf50/1
msgid ""
"Huh? What about it?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/250/0xfaf50/2
msgid ""
"You mumbled that when I first explained about\n"
"Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/0
msgid ""
"Those papers the CIA gave you... Was there any\n"
"data on the Shagohod in there?\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA给你的那些论文里……\n"
"有关于Shagohod的数据吗？\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/1
msgid ""
"Shagohod?\n"
msgstr ""
"Shagohod？\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/2
msgid ""
"A nuclear tank that launches IRBMs.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种发射中程弹道导弹的核坦克。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/3
msgid ""
"It competed against Granin's system for approval.\n"
msgstr ""
"它和格拉宁的系统竞争审批。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/4
msgid ""
"Oh, the thing with the rockets. Designed by a guy\n"
"named... Sokolov, right? ...Heh heh.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，那个带火箭的。设计者叫……\n"
"索科洛夫，对吧？……嘿嘿。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/5
msgid ""
"What's so funny?\n"
msgstr ""
"笑什么？\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/6
msgid ""
"No, I was just remembering some of the\n"
"\"commentary\" Granin added to the Shagohod\n"
"papers.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我只是想起格拉宁在Shagohod\n"
"论文里加的\n"
"一些“评论”。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/7
msgid ""
"You should have seen the way he bad-mouthed it.\n"
msgstr ""
"你真该看看他骂得多难听。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/8
msgid ""
"It was too conservative, too ugly...\n"
msgstr ""
"太保守、太丑……\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/10
msgid ""
"He was so angry when he wrote that he smeared\n"
"up the ink.\n"
msgstr ""
"他写那信时太愤怒，把墨水都\n"
"抹花了。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/11
msgid ""
"And you know how shoddy the paper is over there\n"
"to begin with.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且你知道那边的纸张本来就有多\n"
"粗劣。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/12
msgid ""
"...I'll bet. That's Granin, all right.\n"
msgstr ""
"……信了。是格拉宁。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/13
msgid ""
"Imagine, accelerating the launcher itself to 300\n"
"miles an hour to extend the range of an IRBM...\n"
msgstr ""
"把发射器本身加速到每小时300英里，\n"
"来延长中程弹道导弹射程……\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/14
msgid ""
"As stupid as it sounds, it's a hell of a concept.\n"
msgstr ""
"听着蠢，但想法真够狠。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/15
msgid ""
"Who but the Soviets would think of using a tank as\n"
"the first stage of a rocket?\n"
msgstr ""
"除了苏联人，还有谁会想到用坦克作为\n"
"火箭的第一级？\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/16
msgid ""
"I actually took a cue from the Shagohod when I\n"
"developed the Pupa.\n"
msgstr ""
"我开发蛹式时其实就从\n"
"Shagohod得到启发。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/17
msgid ""
"That hovercraft thing? You stole that one, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"那个气垫的东西？你这也抄了？\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/18
msgid ""
"Give me a little credit! I only borrowed the concept.\n"
"The technology is original.\n"
msgstr ""
"给我点功劳吧！我只是借用了概念。\n"
"技术可是原创的。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/19
msgid ""
"As it turned out,\n"
msgstr ""
"结果呢，\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/20
msgid ""
"hover technology wasn't enough to handle all the\n"
"terrain in Central America.\n"
msgstr ""
"悬停技术不足以应对中美洲的\n"
"所有地形。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/21
msgid ""
"It relied too much on brute force.\n"
msgstr ""
"太依赖蛮力了。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/22
msgid ""
"But the Shagohod was a major threat.\n"
msgstr ""
"但Shagohod是重大威胁。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/23
msgid ""
"That thing could corner like you wouldn't believe -\n"
"built pretty tough, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"那东西转弯快得吓人——\n"
"还特别结实。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/24
msgid ""
"You sure know a lot about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"你倒是挺了解它。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/25
msgid ""
"It almost did me in. I couldn't forget it if I tried.\n"
msgstr ""
"它差点要了我的命，想忘都忘不掉。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/26
msgid ""
"Did you in? ...So you were the one who took it\n"
"down!\n"
msgstr ""
"你参与了吗？……所以就是你把它\n"
"击落的！\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/27
msgid ""
"Wow! You really are amazing.\n"
msgstr ""
"哇！你真厉害。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/28
msgid ""
"I didn't do it alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"不光靠我。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/29
msgid ""
"No, seriously, thank you.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，真的谢了。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/30
msgid ""
"We might not be here today if they'd begun\n"
"mass-producing that thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果他们开始批量生产那东西，我们\n"
"今天可能就不会在这里了。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/31
msgid ""
"Then again, they're hard at work now miniaturizing\n"
"nuclear warheads.\n"
msgstr ""
"话说回来，他们现在正忙着将核弹头\n"
"小型化。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/32
msgid ""
"Pretty soon they won't even need an accelerated\n"
"launcher like the Shagohod.\n"
msgstr ""
"很快他们甚至不需要像Shagohod这样的\n"
"加速发射器了。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfb280/33
msgid ""
"Great. That means they're that much closer to\n"
"being able to launch from anywhere in the world.\n"
msgstr ""
"很好。这意味着他们离\n"
"能在世界任何地方发射又近了一大步。\n"

#: codec/1/251/0xfbe10/0
msgid ""
"Chico called Peace Walker the basilisco.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfbe10/1
msgid ""
"Basilisco? ...Oh, right, Spanish.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfbe10/2
msgid ""
"That's funny.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfbe10/3
msgid ""
"I once used the codename Basilisk for the Peace\n"
"Walker platform myself.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfbe10/5
msgid ""
"The class of lizards called basilisks can walk atop\n"
"any type of terrain.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/251/0xfbe10/6
msgid ""
"In a pinch, they can even stand up on two legs and\n"
"run across water.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 445..1574
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/0
msgid ""
"Peace Walker contains an assembly of two AI pods.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者装有两个AI舱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 1588..2674
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/1
msgid ""
"One of them is the Mammal Pod, which Dr.\n"
"Strangelove developed.\n"
msgstr ""
"其一是哺乳动物舱，由\n"
"Strangelove 博士开发。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 2688..3469
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/2
msgid ""
"The other's the Reptile Pod, which is mine.\n"
msgstr ""
"另一个是爬虫舱，是我做的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 3469..3845
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/3
msgid ""
"What's the difference?\n"
msgstr ""
"有什么区别？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 3845..4848
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/4
msgid ""
"The Reptile Pod is the attitude control AI.\n"
msgstr ""
"爬虫舱是姿态控制AI。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 4904..5795
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/5
msgid ""
"If it's destroyed, Peace Walker grinds to a halt.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦被毁，和平行者就会瘫痪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 5823..7258
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/6
msgid ""
"The Mammal Pod is responsible for making the\n"
"decisions regarding nuclear retaliation.\n"
msgstr ""
"哺乳动物舱负责做出\n"
"有关核报复的决策。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 7258..9013
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/7
msgid ""
"Reflex and thought... One is the brainstem and\n"
"cerebellum, the other the cerebrum.\n"
msgstr ""
"反射与思考……一个是脑干和\n"
"小脑，另一个是大脑。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 9013..9975
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/8
msgid ""
"So the one that houses the will of The Boss...\n"
msgstr ""
"那么承载THE BOSS意志的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_000_0
#. timeline 9975..10574
#: codec/1/252/0xfc530/9
msgid ""
"...Would be the Mammal Pod.\n"
msgstr ""
"……就是哺乳舱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 445..1212
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/0
msgid ""
"We call it the \"Reptile Pod\" for a reason.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们叫它爬虫舱是有原因的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 1212..2605
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/1
msgid ""
"The parts of our brains that govern basic life and\n"
"reflex developed ages ago,\n"
msgstr ""
"我们大脑掌管基本生命和\n"
"反射的部分很久前就发育了，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 2619..3301
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/2
msgid ""
"when our ancestors were still reptiles.\n"
msgstr ""
"那时祖先还是爬行动物。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 3329..3789
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/3
msgid ""
"We were reptiles?\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是爬行动物？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 3803..4653
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/4
msgid ""
"Well, only at one stage of our evolution.\n"
msgstr ""
"只是在进化的某个阶段。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 4736..5739
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/5
msgid ""
"The theory was proposed by the neuroscientist\n"
"Paul MacLean.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一理论由神经科学家\n"
"Paul MacLean 提出。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 5935..7453
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/7
msgid ""
"The reptile brain corresponds to the brainstem and\n"
"basal ganglia in our brain.\n"
msgstr ""
"爬行动物脑对应我们大脑中的脑干和\n"
"基底神经节。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 7551..8568
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/8
msgid ""
"The Reptile Pod also incorporates the functions of\n"
"the cerebellum.\n"
msgstr ""
"爬行动物舱也整合了\n"
"小脑的功能。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 8568..9626
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/9
msgid ""
"So basically, it's the deep parts of the brain.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以基本上，它是大脑深层。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_010_0
#. timeline 9626..10351
#: codec/1/252/0xfc8d0/10
msgid ""
"Dr. Strangelove came up with the name.\n"
msgstr ""
"斯特兰奇洛夫博士起的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 445..1323
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/0
msgid ""
"The part of our brain that developed after we\n"
"became mammals\n"
msgstr ""
"我们大脑中在\n"
"成为哺乳动物后发育的部分\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 1323..2145
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/1
msgid ""
"is responsible for high-level brain functions.\n"
msgstr ""
"负责高级脑功能。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 2145..2438
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/2
msgid ""
"Such as?\n"
msgstr ""
"比如？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 2452..3580
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/3
msgid ""
"Such as intelligence, judgment... even love.\n"
msgstr ""
"比如智力、判断……甚至爱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 3580..4235
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/4
msgid ""
"That's high-level, all right.\n"
msgstr ""
"确实很高层。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 4249..5600
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/5
msgid ""
"Location-wise, the mammal brain is on the outside\n"
"of the reptile brain.\n"
msgstr ""
"从位置上看，哺乳动物脑位于爬行动物脑的\n"
"外侧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 5628..6311
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/6
msgid ""
"The cerebral cortex is part of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"大脑皮层是其中一部分。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 6325..7509
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/7
msgid ""
"I think it's very telling that Dr. Strangelove named\n"
"her pod \"Mammal.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得很能说明问题的是，Strangelove 博士把\n"
"她的舱体命名为“哺乳动物”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0160_020_0
#. timeline 7565..8749
#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/8
msgid ""
"It's almost like she wants it to be more than just\n"
"an advanced AI\n"
msgstr ""
"简直就像她希望它不仅仅是一个\n"
"先进的人工智能\n"

#: codec/1/252/0xfcc90/9
msgid ""
"- what she really wants is for it to have a mind of\n"
"its own.\n"
msgstr ""
"——她真正想要的是让它拥有自己的\n"
"思想。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1825
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/0
msgid ""
"Snake, how much do you know about the U.S.\n"
"homeland air defense network?\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，你对美国\n"
"本土防空网络了解多少？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2702
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/1
msgid ""
"I don't know much about what goes on up in the\n"
"sky.\n"
msgstr ""
"我对天上\n"
"发生的事情不太了解。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 2800..3970
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/2
msgid ""
"What I do know is that NORAD tracks Santa Claus\n"
"on its radar.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道 NORAD 会在雷达上\n"
"追踪圣诞老人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 3970..5099
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/3
msgid ""
"Ha! Nice one. I didn't know you were a comedian,\n"
"too!\n"
msgstr ""
"哈！说得好。没想到你还是\n"
"喜剧演员！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 5099..5865
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/4
msgid ""
"Huh? No, I'm serious...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯？不，真的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 6185..6882
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/5
msgid ""
"It's true. NORAD tracks his...\n"
msgstr ""
"真的。北美防空司令部追踪他……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 7606..8721
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/6
msgid ""
"Listen to me! Every December, they set up a\n"
"hotline and...\n"
msgstr ""
"听我说！每年十二月，他们都会设立一条\n"
"热线，然后……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 9585..10490
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/7
msgid ""
"OK, OK, I get it.\n"
msgstr ""
"好，懂了\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 10490..11103
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/8
msgid ""
"...He's real, I tell ya.\n"
msgstr ""
"……他真的存在。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_000_0
#. timeline 11145..11939
#: codec/1/253/0xfd020/9
msgid ""
"He... used to bring me presents and...\n"
msgstr ""
"他……送过我礼物\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/0
msgid ""
"OK, Snakey. As all good little boys know,\n"
msgstr ""
"好了，小蛇。乖孩子都知道，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 1476..2772
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/1
msgid ""
"keeping tabs on Santa Claus is a very important\n"
"job for NORAD.\n"
msgstr ""
"监视圣诞老人是 NORAD 的\n"
"重要工作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 2772..3134
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/2
msgid ""
"Ugh...\n"
msgstr ""
"呃……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 3148..4527
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/3
msgid ""
"But they also have another mission - the one they\n"
"were created for.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他们还有另一项任务，他们\n"
"就是为此而生。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 4555..5085
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/4
msgid ""
"And the system they set up for that...\n"
msgstr ""
"而他们为此建立的系统……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 5085..5767
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/5
msgid ""
"Has been hijacked by Coldman.\n"
msgstr ""
"已被科尔德曼劫持。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 5767..6534
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/6
msgid ""
"...You mean Peace Walker's fake data\n"
"transmissions?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你是指 Peace Walker 的虚假数据\n"
"传输？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 6534..8303
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/7
msgid ""
"NORAD's early warning system is composed of DSP\n"
"satellite-mounted infrared sensors,\n"
msgstr ""
"NORAD 的预警系统由 DSP\n"
"卫星搭载的红外传感器组成，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 8331..9529
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/8
msgid ""
"and an array of surveillance radar stations across\n"
"North America.\n"
msgstr ""
"以及遍布北美的一系列\n"
"监视雷达站。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 9557..10616
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/9
msgid ""
"The network sends out warnings to NORAD at\n"
"Cheyenne Mountain,\n"
msgstr ""
"网络会向夏延山的北美防空司令部\n"
"发警报，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 10616..11424
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/10
msgid ""
"where the data undergoes human evaluation.\n"
msgstr ""
"数据在那里由人工评估。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 11438..12831
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/11
msgid ""
"Peace Walker, on the other hand, has to make its\n"
"retaliation decisions autonomously.\n"
msgstr ""
"而和平行者必须自主做出\n"
"报复决策。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 12859..14628
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/12
msgid ""
"So it's set up to automatically receive the same\n"
"data as NORAD through covert channels.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以它设定为通过秘密渠道\n"
"自动接收北美防空司令部同数据。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 14656..16397
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/13
msgid ""
"Those channels were also used on the test\n"
"platform to telemeter the AI's decision-making.\n"
msgstr ""
"测试平台上也用这些渠道\n"
"遥测AI的决策过程。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 16481..17735
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/14
msgid ""
"Peace Walker reversed the system to transmit a\n"
"fake warning\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者把系统反过来，发送了一条\n"
"假警报\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 17735..19017
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/15
msgid ""
"about incoming nuclear missiles outside the usual\n"
"exercise schedule.\n"
msgstr ""
"谎称有核导弹来袭，且不在\n"
"常规演习时间表内。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 19072..20466
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/16
msgid ""
"I mean, the system could have used better\n"
"safeguarding, nobody's going to argue with that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我是说，这系统的防护本该更好，\n"
"这点没人会否认。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0170_010_0
#. timeline 20493..22444
#: codec/1/253/0xfd370/17
msgid ""
"But cracking the AI - that seemed unimaginable.\n"
"And you can see what happened.\n"
msgstr ""
"但破解AI——那简直难以想象。\n"
"结果你也看到了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 445..1337
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/0
msgid ""
"Hey Doc, what was that you were smoking in the\n"
"lab?\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿博士，你刚在实验室抽的是\n"
"什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 1351..2006
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/1
msgid ""
"It looked like a cigarette, but it wasn't lit.\n"
msgstr ""
"看着像香烟，但没点着。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 2284..3650
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/2
msgid ""
"It's an electronic cigarette. I designed it myself.\n"
"Pretty neat, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"是电子烟。我自己设计的。\n"
"挺不错吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 3650..4486
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/3
msgid ""
"Electronic. Cigarette.\n"
msgstr ""
"电子。烟。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 4500..5976
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/4
msgid ""
"Yep. A liquid in the filter that turns into vapor, and\n"
"you inhale the microparticles.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。滤嘴里的液体变成蒸汽，\n"
"你吸入这些微粒。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 5976..6408
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/5
msgid ""
"So that was vapor.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是蒸汽。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 6422..7634
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/6
msgid ""
"I'd actually rather be smoking normal cigarettes,\n"
"but not in that room...\n"
msgstr ""
"其实我更想抽普通烟，\n"
"但不能在那屋里抽……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8832
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/7
msgid ""
"The smoke would wreck the precision equipment in\n"
"there, ruin all its wiring.\n"
msgstr ""
"烟雾会毁掉里面的精密设备，\n"
"弄坏所有线路。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 8860..10267
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/8
msgid ""
"But the vapor is just steam. It doesn't contain tar\n"
"or anything like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"但蒸汽只是水汽。不含焦油\n"
"之类的东西。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 10365..11020
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/9
msgid ""
"So I can smoke it in the lab with no worries.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以我在实验室里可以放心抽。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 11020..11284
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/10
msgid ""
"Nice.\n"
msgstr ""
"不错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 11284..11591
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/11
msgid ""
"Want to try one?\n"
msgstr ""
"要试一根？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0200_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12246
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/12
msgid ""
"Nah, I'll stick with cigars.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我抽雪茄。\n"

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/14
msgid ""
"I don't like imitations - the real thing's always\n"
"better.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不喜欢仿制品——真货总是\n"
"更好。\n"

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/15
msgid ""
"OK. But you know, sooner or later smoking's going\n"
"to become\n"
msgstr ""
"行。不过迟早有一天\n"
"吸烟会在全世界\n"

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/16
msgid ""
"very unfashionable across the world. It hurts you\n"
"and those around you.\n"
msgstr ""
"变得很不流行。它害己\n"
"又害人。\n"

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/17
msgid ""
"Electronic cigarettes might not seem so bad then.\n"
msgstr ""
"那电子烟也许没那么糟。\n"

#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/18
msgid ""
"Yeah, when that happens, I'll think about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，等真到那一步再说吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 445..1309
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/0
msgid ""
"You said your dad was involved in the Manhattan\n"
"Project, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"你说过你父亲参与过曼哈顿\n"
"计划，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 1476..2117
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/2
msgid ""
"And you think that's why you can't walk?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得这就是你不能走路的原因？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 2117..3538
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/3
msgid ""
"...I dunno. Actually, you know, probably not.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不知道。其实，大概不是。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4500
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/4
msgid ""
"So far nobody's found evidence that exposure to\n"
"radiation\n"
msgstr ""
"至今没人找到证据证明父母\n"
"受辐射\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 4500..5349
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/5
msgid ""
"in parents causes genetic defects in children,\n"
msgstr ""
"会导致子女基因缺陷，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 5377..6770
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/6
msgid ""
"except for those exposed in the womb...\n"
"Epidemiologically speaking, anyway.\n"
msgstr ""
"除了在母体内受辐射的……\n"
"从流行病学上讲，是这样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 6840..7774
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/7
msgid ""
"That's the conclusion of the Atomic Bomb Casualty\n"
"Commission?\n"
msgstr ""
"这是原子弹伤害调查委员会\n"
"的结论？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 7801..9139
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/8
msgid ""
"Right. The ABCC commenced its study immediately\n"
"after the war.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。ABCC在战后立刻\n"
"开始了研究。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 9153..9599
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/9
msgid ""
"And it's still ongoing.\n"
msgstr ""
"至今仍在继续。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 9613..10365
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/10
msgid ""
"Even now, 30 years later...\n"
msgstr ""
"30年后依然如此……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 10379..11396
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/11
msgid ""
"The effects of radiation exposure last a long time.\n"
msgstr ""
"辐射的影响会持续很久。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 11479..12413
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/12
msgid ""
"I'm guessing it'll be another ten years before we\n"
"get a real verdict on\n"
msgstr ""
"我猜还得再过十年才能\n"
"得出真正的结论，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 12413..12956
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/13
msgid ""
"whether it affects genes.\n"
msgstr ""
"它是否影响基因。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 12970..14029
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/14
msgid ""
"Granted, it's the most massive study anybody's\n"
"ever done.\n"
msgstr ""
"诚然，这是史上规模最大的\n"
"研究。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 14099..14907
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/15
msgid ""
"But that's really all it is - a study.\n"
msgstr ""
"但说到底只是研究。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 14935..16467
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/16
msgid ""
"The ABCC brought in bomb victims and ran tests\n"
"on them, but they didn't treat them.\n"
msgstr ""
"ABCC把受害者带来做检查，\n"
"却不给他们治疗。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 16495..17373
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/17
msgid ""
"Really... them too, huh...\n"
msgstr ""
"真的……他们也一样啊……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 17401..18432
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/18
msgid ""
"At any rate, that's what my father made me believe\n"
"when I was growing up...\n"
msgstr ""
"总之，我从小就被父亲\n"
"灌输了这些……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 18432..19713
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/19
msgid ""
"Maybe it was tough for your dad to explain. Ever\n"
"think of that?\n"
msgstr ""
"也许你父亲很难开口解释。\n"
"你想过吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 19713..20981
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/20
msgid ""
"Yeah, maybe. But this is my problem now, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许吧。但这是我的问题，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 21037..22165
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/21
msgid ""
"I have to face the nukes head on, whether I like it\n"
"or not.\n"
msgstr ""
"不管愿不愿意，我都得\n"
"直面核武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 22221..23182
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/22
msgid ""
"My creations are being used for the wrong\n"
"purposes.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的发明被用在了\n"
"错误的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 23266..24506
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/23
msgid ""
"The onus is on me to stop it somehow. Help me,\n"
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"我有责任阻止它。帮帮我，\n"
"SNAKE。\n"

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/0
msgid ""
"Hey! As long as I'm here at Mother Base, why not\n"
"assign me to the R&D team?\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿！既然我在母亲基地，不如\n"
"把我分到研发团队？\n"

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/1
msgid ""
"You could use a guy like me.\n"
msgstr ""
"用得上我这样的人。\n"

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/2
msgid ""
"Glad to have you on board. I'm sure Kaz is, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"欢迎加入。卡兹肯定也是。\n"

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/3
msgid ""
"Once I've got the necessary materials and design\n"
"specs together,\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦我准备好了必要的材料和设计\n"
"规格，\n"

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/4
msgid ""
"I should be able to start building you that bipedal\n"
"weapon platform.\n"
msgstr ""
"我就能开始为你建造那个双足\n"
"武器平台了。\n"

#: codec/1/254/0xfe8b0/5
msgid ""
"Nothing would make me happier than for my\n"
"research to help put a stop to Peace Walker.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有什么能比我的\n"
"研究有助于阻止和平行者更让我高兴的了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/0
msgid ""
"So this Dr. Strangelove was at NASA?\n"
msgstr ""
"这位斯特兰奇洛夫博士在NASA待过？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 1393..2702
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/1
msgid ""
"Yeah. Well, actually, Strangelove left for DARPA not\n"
"long after I joined.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，其实我加入后不久\n"
"斯特兰奇洛夫就去DARPA了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 2702..3859
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/2
msgid ""
"And then the two of you ended up back together\n"
"doing research in Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""
"然后你们两个最终又在一起\n"
"在哥斯达黎加做研究了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 3942..5322
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/3
msgid ""
"Not exactly \"together.\" We coordinated on a few\n"
"things,\n"
msgstr ""
"不全是“一起”。我们协调过一些\n"
"事，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 5322..6255
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/4
msgid ""
"but the research projects themselves were\n"
"separate from each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"但研究项目本身是\n"
"彼此独立的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7383
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/5
msgid ""
"We had it worked out so that Dr. Strangelove\n"
"handled the Mammal Pod,\n"
msgstr ""
"我们已经安排好了，让斯特兰奇洛夫博士\n"
"处理哺乳动物舱，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 7411..8219
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/6
msgid ""
"Peace Walker's cerebrum, while I did the rest.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者的大脑，其余归我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 8219..9222
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/7
msgid ""
"That letter - something to do with your research...?\n"
msgstr ""
"那封信——和你的研究有关？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 9222..10170
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/8
msgid ""
"Huh? Er, no, it's, uh...\n"
msgstr ""
"啊？呃，不，那是……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 10198..11382
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/9
msgid ""
"Y-yeah, it's a report. Research findings.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，是份报告。研究结果。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 11382..12608
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/10
msgid ""
"Research findings? Anything in there we could use\n"
"against Peace Walker?\n"
msgstr ""
"研究结果？里面有什么可以用来\n"
"对抗和平行者的吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 12608..13221
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/11
msgid ""
"N-nothing! Nothing at all!\n"
msgstr ""
"没、没有！什么都没有！\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0230_000_0
#. timeline 13235..14308
#: codec/1/254/0xfeb50/12
msgid ""
"Just don't read it, OK? Promise me you won't!\n"
msgstr ""
"别看它，确定？答应我别看！\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/0
msgid ""
"Did you give that letter to Dr. Strangelove?\n"
msgstr ""
"信给斯特兰奇洛夫博士了吗？\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/1
msgid ""
"...Uh, no.\n"
msgstr ""
"……呃，没有。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/2
msgid ""
"Why not? I gave it to you for a reason. It's highly\n"
"important information.\n"
msgstr ""
"为啥不？我给你有原因。这信息\n"
"非常重要。\n"

#: codec/1/255/0xff000/3
msgid ""
"Sorry. I didn't exactly have an opportunity to play\n"
"postman.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉。我并没有机会\n"
"当邮差。\n"
